#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082971 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8922ab07-5ac7-5f85-bfee-c30de7f4024a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Parametric Curve"}] :question/id #uuid "15c029df-b002-51cc-87db-a94d40a02771" :question/math-academy-id "e-595" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n$x=\\cos{t}, \\quad y=\\sin{t}, \\qquad 0\\leq t<2\\pi$, calculate $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/798/Source/Images/0f8bfc82b98e63e586e9d2e96d1acc5d.png)" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y$, we get\n\n$$\nx'(t) = -\\sin{t}, \\qquad y'(t)=\\cos{t}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{\\cos t}{-\\sin t} = -\\cot t\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082972 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bda136-40a9-576a-b85c-4d4ebefaeb27" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parametric Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/id #uuid "148e5378-9177-59ba-9b1e-3633c940babd" :question/math-academy-id "e-596" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n$x=te^t, \\quad y=e^{-t}, \\qquad -\\infty < t <\\infty$,\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=1$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y$, we get\n\n$$\nx'(t) = e^t + te^t = (1+t)e^t, \\qquad y'(t)=-e^{-t}\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\frac{\\mathrm{d} y}{\\mathrm{d} x} & = \\frac{- {e}^{- t}}{( 1 + t ) {e}^{t}} \\\\  & = - \\frac{1}{( 1 + t ) {e}^{2 t}} .\\end{array}$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=1$, the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}{\\frac{\\mathrm{d} y}{\\mathrm{d} x} |}_{t = 1} & = - \\frac{1}{{e}^{2 ( 1 )} ( 1 + 1 )} \\\\  & = - \\frac{1}{2 {e}^{2}} .\\end{array}$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262934 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bda136-40a9-576a-b85c-4d4ebefaeb27" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parametric Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35fd903a-d729-526b-bb61-9607a7ea00fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262936} {:answer/id #uuid "65e7f290-b617-5197-a61e-57d0ea809855" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262937} {:answer/id #uuid "788d8d49-dce4-50ed-af51-f63d12773e6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262938} {:answer/id #uuid "ec559a54-c83a-548a-b6cd-9cf419698065" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262939} {:answer/id #uuid "945e0974-538c-534c-8e64-b72277388871" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec559a54-c83a-548a-b6cd-9cf419698065" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262939} :answer-field/id #uuid "963457c2-cfbd-557d-bf67-09ed76aa13de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262935}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3a94c8b6-af79-5573-a1c6-6e6e990a28cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-102922" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,y={sin}^{2}⁡t,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{12}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{12},$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262941 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bda136-40a9-576a-b85c-4d4ebefaeb27" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parametric Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9a4279b-0f5c-5b97-9e83-b00052f39697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262943} {:answer/id #uuid "92aa918d-c8de-5fbe-9553-727cd6f9c9fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262944} {:answer/id #uuid "323a20cf-27d3-5675-88ae-ee3868536fac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262945} {:answer/id #uuid "0437357f-68d7-5270-8cfd-e7be653596c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262946} {:answer/id #uuid "3a692b14-0543-5852-9204-5dce1f445d61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a692b14-0543-5852-9204-5dce1f445d61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262947} :answer-field/id #uuid "9959376b-5bc9-5d3a-9579-da6049626b2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262942}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "16fc9f31-33f6-5972-9529-3afa5f1e1dc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-15465" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-1}{1+0} \\\\  & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262948 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bda136-40a9-576a-b85c-4d4ebefaeb27" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parametric Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fc57ba9-c166-5c1e-837f-4646755994d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{8e}{27}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262950} {:answer/id #uuid "48c7f3ca-6131-550c-8143-08ab3e1a15c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{8e}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262951} {:answer/id #uuid "7c99c21d-890e-534d-84e3-a21b6c050b2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{27e}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262952} {:answer/id #uuid "434a3446-cd9c-57c9-938d-f0b5366df13f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{9e}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262953} {:answer/id #uuid "6dc7e053-d1d4-575f-bd42-f44eb987debe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{9e}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c99c21d-890e-534d-84e3-a21b6c050b2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{27e}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262952} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca4903a3-8a91-5e14-a591-a110458c9f28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262949}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "56044f7d-8044-5dcb-9e59-27af5ccb11e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-15475" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx={e}^{1/t},\\,y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-1}},\\,1<t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}{e}^{1/t},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{t}{({t}^{2}-1)^{3/2}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{(-\\frac{t}{({t}^{2}-1)^{3/2}})}{(-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}{e}^{1/t})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{3}{e}^{-1/t}}{({t}^{2}-1)^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=2,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{{2}^{3}{e}^{-1/2}}{({2}^{2}-1)^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{{3}^{3/2}\\sqrt{e}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{27e}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262955 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8922ab07-5ac7-5f85-bfee-c30de7f4024a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Parametric Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "739890dd-80a1-5792-b127-7200eb833cff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262957} {:answer/id #uuid "f3f44842-47bf-5477-a1aa-297338f081a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262958} {:answer/id #uuid "d8c91dec-b8f6-5ed9-9ab7-8e0dffe93718" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262959} {:answer/id #uuid "bf8a1dd7-09b0-507a-ba14-0b7c7ed35dbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262960} {:answer/id #uuid "f71a3229-0f8c-5a8d-8583-eb2af6ff898b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "739890dd-80a1-5792-b127-7200eb833cff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262957} :answer-field/id #uuid "b44383b4-11f8-51bc-bcac-0b4f94af9000" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262956}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a11f695c-004e-57f4-b1f5-cd09434f69e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-20851" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=2\\sqrt{t},\\,y=12t+1,\\,0\\le t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=12.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{12}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}}=12\\sqrt{t}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=1$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =12\\sqrt{1} \\\\  & =12\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262962 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8922ab07-5ac7-5f85-bfee-c30de7f4024a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Parametric Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e43e99e-718a-5c86-b678-70658ef39a88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262964} {:answer/id #uuid "4dba3a05-92fc-5355-8b0c-383f8aa219c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262965} {:answer/id #uuid "a336f0d3-e7dd-5861-96d6-b076eb40ace7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262966} {:answer/id #uuid "6df64199-19a6-5cdf-9d95-abcb09a30ca5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262967} {:answer/id #uuid "190e3513-48de-5f61-9b0c-10fd1565b1fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a336f0d3-e7dd-5861-96d6-b076eb40ace7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262966} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5d59da5-e499-5d62-bd44-d06a4ae2d2b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262963}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "086f12ac-4759-5fbb-bb3d-6ee45cc6ce1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-20988" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949328/assets/0b77bdde611689095cdea6a3a08ce9828b9e20040283dc0c251250538a5cfba3.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx=3{t}^{2}-2t,\\,y={t}^{2}-1,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=6t-2,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2t}{6t-2}=\\frac{t}{3t-1}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=2$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{2}{3(2)-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{6-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083522 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bda136-40a9-576a-b85c-4d4ebefaeb27" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parametric Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5ec03d0-7322-5f58-b3ae-7b1eb9ccc6d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8e^{5}}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080631} {:answer/id #uuid "f9cb97db-187f-5526-931e-cbc2f5e02dea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5e^{4}}{\\sqrt{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080632} {:answer/id #uuid "03709d50-0fa9-5eb1-be2a-12bd75719399" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{3}}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080633} {:answer/id #uuid "704dc8a6-7814-52e4-88a8-c81f04287f3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4e^{5}}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080634} {:answer/id #uuid "7da078bf-46dd-5f1d-b83f-becf7a45d04e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8e^{5}}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5ec03d0-7322-5f58-b3ae-7b1eb9ccc6d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8e^{5}}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080631} :answer-field/id #uuid "037556c8-fd10-5e4a-b6e0-378e32bb8f71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080630}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f252b1a9-57b3-57ad-97f5-a61e75b56356" :question/math-academy-id "q-20991" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$x = \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}, y = \\frac{e^{t}}{2t}, - \\infty  < t < \\infty $,\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t = 5$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{-3/2},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{2t{e}^{t}-2{e}^{t}}{4{t}^{2}}=\\frac{{e}^{t}(t-1)}{2{t}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{{e}^{t}(t-1)}{2{t}^{2}}\\cdot (-4{t}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2{e}^{t}(t-1)}{\\sqrt{t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=5,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =-\\,\\frac{2{e}^{5}(5-1)}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{2{e}^{5}\\cdot 4}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{8{e}^{5}}{\\sqrt{5}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262969 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bda136-40a9-576a-b85c-4d4ebefaeb27" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parametric Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "959affd4-d5f0-5fff-b1d2-e6f856077e47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262971} {:answer/id #uuid "d7c0bed7-a207-5331-8131-6ff7423443b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7c0bed7-a207-5331-8131-6ff7423443b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262972} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ef2b9f2-2901-50b6-91bc-9e88c0f87ff0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262970}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9cc31f35-4916-5f32-a8c9-fe9e2d10f162" :question/math-academy-id "q-348303" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949328/assets/59f053b9a122018d78cd9c30f5a53cd67cd2ff645d02ccb6d311e6183e081102.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx={t}^{3}+2{t}^{2},\\,y={t}^{2},\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\nshown above, calculate the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{t}^{2}+4t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{2t}{3{t}^{2}+4t} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3t+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=2,$ the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{dy}{dx}\\,{|}_{t\\,=\\,2} & =\\frac{2}{3(2)+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{6+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262973 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8922ab07-5ac7-5f85-bfee-c30de7f4024a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Parametric Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc1b76fb-62f5-5fe4-970b-d337f5125634" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc1b76fb-62f5-5fe4-970b-d337f5125634" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262975} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ce3f65f-2ff0-5ad3-9dd8-0d12e0552286" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262974}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6f44a7e1-514a-5573-bc6d-02d50696e90b" :question/math-academy-id "q-353341" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949328/assets/1817c65aea37112d93f2935801a0e7dcd654706a72f729810272f48e95d39665.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nfind the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}{|}_{t\\,=\\,\\pi /6}=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{(-2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)}{10\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡2t.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262976 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8922ab07-5ac7-5f85-bfee-c30de7f4024a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Parametric Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edefa64c-fcbd-59cb-9d3c-9be1fbec8796" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262978} {:answer/id #uuid "5d8106ae-4c2f-5db9-977f-aeb769344f5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262979} {:answer/id #uuid "a65fc94c-0deb-5a29-a6ff-e6e6aad0bed7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262980} {:answer/id #uuid "320945e9-703f-5067-a062-14673ea486c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262981} {:answer/id #uuid "0a9a48f7-eb5f-5641-8a82-77104ffe3305" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262982}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "320945e9-703f-5067-a062-14673ea486c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262981} :answer-field/id #uuid "7624c062-786d-5f09-942a-66bf33c08d66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262977}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1990413b-418b-52e9-8b02-51eb17f5b4b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-6816" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx={e}^{2t},\\,y=({t}^{2}-1){e}^{-t},\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2{e}^{2t},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=(1+2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{(1+2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}}{2{e}^{2t}}=\\frac{1}{2}(1+2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-3t}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=1$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+2(1)-(1)^{2}){e}^{-3(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+2-1){e}^{-3} \\\\  & ={e}^{-3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262983 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8922ab07-5ac7-5f85-bfee-c30de7f4024a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Parametric Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e385bf7e-c972-5a34-9afd-9c71395037b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262985} {:answer/id #uuid "5abc5a1c-93cb-5968-afe5-6138865a6ae2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262986} {:answer/id #uuid "f8f6723c-d43d-5f93-85ed-a818c30ba834" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262987} {:answer/id #uuid "a5ebbcf8-2d88-56c2-87ee-410104c80e22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262988} {:answer/id #uuid "e4e87762-ab3c-595d-95c8-e17b533ffa21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5ebbcf8-2d88-56c2-87ee-410104c80e22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262988} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5a22319-9eb8-56ab-b60c-fa724f5d5ee7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262984}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b50faac3-57b3-5534-a1d3-8f76087cb51c" :question/math-academy-id "q-6836" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=12\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=15\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\n calculate $\\frac{dy}{dx}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\theta )}{{x}^{′}(\\theta )}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(\\theta )=12\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,{y}^{′}(\\theta )=-15\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{-15\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{12\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }=-\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}]}
